The original's plugin folder is a portable manifest and an mcp.json: no code,
no skills, no scripts. It names one hosted MCP server behind a browser
sign-in with an emailed code, and that server answers ten tools over the
Projects, followed accounts, Hits, plan usage, collection runs and Instagram
transcripts of an Onda account. This cell reaches the same data through the
REST API the same repository documents for its skills in the `skills/`
folder: one host, https://app.getonda.ru, authorized with an X-API-Key header
instead of OAuth. Each of the ten tools keeps the original tool's job, under
the name onda_<job>, and one /onda command runs the free reads from the
keyboard.

Left out, and why: the MCP transport and its OAuth sign-in, because a cell
cannot open a browser for an emailed code, so the credential is an API key
from the same account; the manifest name `onda` as the system name, because
Nodecode's cells are named nodecode-<slug> (the package nickname, the
command and the manual topic are still `onda`); the operation_id a repeat
call reuses, which the REST run endpoints this cell calls do not take, so a
second run spends again — the manual says so.
